Objective: Setting up CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions or Jenkins, Automated testing 
and deployment, Integrating with Docker.
Required Software / Tools: Docker Desktop, Python, VSCode, GITHUB.
Procedure:
Step1: Login to VSCode, open new folder name Exp5 and create app.py file with 
basic python program as below.
def is_palindrome(word: str) -> bool:
 cleaned = word.lower().replace(" ", "")
 return cleaned == cleaned[::-1]
if __name__ == "__main__":
 user_input = input("Enter a word: ")
 if is_palindrome(user_input):
 print(f" '{user_input}' is a palindrome!")
 else:
 print(f" '{user_input}' is not a palindrome.")
Step2: Test the python code locally 
python app.py
Step3: create a test code with name test_app.py
import app
def test_palindrome_true():
 assert app.is_palindrome("madam") is True
 assert app.is_palindrome("racecar") is True
def test_palindrome_false():
 assert app.is_palindrome("hello") is False
 assert app.is_palindrome("python") is False
step4: Test pytest locally
pip install pytest
python -m pytest
step5: Create requirements.txt with below contents 
pytest
Step6: Create Docker file with below contents name it Dockerfile
FROM python:3.10-slim
WORKDIR /app
COPY requirements.txt .
RUN pip install -r requirements.txt
COPY . .
CMD ["python", "app.py"]
Stpe7: Build and Test the Docker Container
docker build -t palindrome-app .
docker run -it palindrome-app
Step 8: Create CI/CD pipeline using GITHUB Actions with name ci.yml under 
i.
From terminal run below command 
mkdir -p .github/workflows
ii.
Navigate to workflow directory and create ci.yml with below contents
name: CI/CD Pipeline
on:
 push:
 branches: [ "main" ]
 pull_request:
 branches: [ "main" ]
jobs:
 build-test:
 runs-on: ubuntu-latest
 steps:
 - name: Checkout code
 uses: actions/checkout@v3
 - name: Set up Python
 uses: actions/setup-python@v4
 with:
 python-version: "3.10
 name: Install dependencies
 run: |
 pip install -r requirements.txt
 - name: Run tests
 run: python -m pytest
 docker-build:
 runs-on: ubuntu-latest
 needs: build-test
 steps:
 - name: Checkout code
 uses: actions/checkout@v3
 - name: Build Docker image
 run: docker build -t palindrome-app .
